    apply: "Write down three personal boundaries for friendships with the opposite sex and share them with a mature friend or mentor. Remove or avoid media that stirs lust. If you have fallen, confess to God and seek help. Memorise 1 Timothy 5:2.",
    activity: "Read 1 Timothy 5:1-2 and 1 Thessalonians 4:3-8. In same-sex groups, discuss practical boundaries and temptations frankly, then report general conclusions. Pray for purity and for those who are struggling.",
    takeHome: "Read 1 Timothy 5:1-16, 1 Thessalonians 4:1-12, Proverbs 5 and Romans 13:8-14. Write your boundaries and a prayer for purity. Memorise 1 Timothy 5:2.",
    prayer: "Thank God for the gift of sexuality in its proper place. Ask for purity of heart and wise boundaries. Pray for those who feel ashamed and for healing.",
    teacher: "This is sensitive. Separate groups by sex for discussion if appropriate and use trained leaders. Keep language respectful, factual and age-appropriate. Follow safeguarding procedures if a disclosure of abuse arises. Avoid shaming those with past experiences. Emphasise grace.",
    assess: "Weekly check: ask learners to give two practical boundaries that support purity.",
    mcq1: ["How does 1 Timothy 5:2 say to treat younger women?", ["As sisters, in all purity", "As objects", "As enemies", "As strangers"], 0, "As sisters in purity."],
    mcq2: ["What is God's will according to 1 Thessalonians 4:3?", ["Your sanctification: that you abstain from sexual immorality", "Wealth", "Fame", "Silence"], 0, "Sanctification and purity."],
